# Tracer: uniform numeric Obj semantics for To-Lean.
#
# Rejected design:
#   z Z -> a native Lean integer binder
#   z / 2 -> (z : Q) / (2 : Q)
# That changes one Litex Obj into several carrier-specific target terms.
#
# Selected ABI:
#   symbols and numerals keep one structural spelling;
#   z / 2 -> z / 2;
#   Z and Q remain standard-set membership facts about those objects.

# The same `n + 1` object can have several proved memberships.
forall n N:
    n + 1 $in N
    n + 1 $in Z

# Neither membership changes the spelling of `z - 1` or `z / 2`.
forall z Z:
    z - 1 $in Z
    z / 2 $in Q

# Mixed membership evidence likewise leaves each object unchanged.
forall z Z, q Q:
    z + q $in Q
    z / 2 + q $in Q

# A natural result for subtraction needs the verifier's lower-bound evidence.
forall n N+:
    n - 1 $in N

# Nearest rejected boundary (kept as a comment because examples must pass):
# forall n N:
#     n - 1 $in N
#
# That statement is rejected by Litex. A backend must preserve this boundary
# through LitexObj subtraction laws rather than assigning `n` a temporary
# native type or changing the canonical `n - 1` object.
#
# Source gate:
# target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/05_compiler_interop/to_lean_numeric_obj_abi.lit
#
# Implementation boundary:
# src/to_lean/math_collections.md#numeric-object-abi
